              <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,570.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,550.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,550.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,550.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,550.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SAHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,554.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,555.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,555.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    MEST OS Is the Digital Operating System Every Fuel Retail Station Needs —Obinna Joshua Igwe\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    MEST OS is an all-in-one retail operations platform built for the downstream oil and gas sector. It centralises the management of single and multi-station fuel retail networks. The platform centralises reporting into one system, reducing reliance on multiple communication channels.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/mest-os-is-the-digital-operating-system-every-fuel-retail-station-needs-obinna-joshua-igwe\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Five Things to Know About Petroleumprice.ng Awards Nomination\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Petroleumprice.ng Recognition & Awards 2026 nomination process is currently open. Participants can nominate individuals and organisations across six categories in Nigeria's downstream petroleum industry. Nominations close on September 15, 2026 and all entries must be submitted before the deadline. Top five nominees in each category will qualify for the next stage of the process.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/five-things-to-know-about-petroleumpriceng-awards-nomination\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iran Sets Six Conditions for Reopening Strait of Hormuz\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iran has signalled that the Strait of Hormuz will remain closed unless the United States meets a set of six conditions. The conditions include military operations, sanctions, compensation and access to Iranian funds.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iran-sets-six-conditions-for-reopening-strait-of-hormuz\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Citi Raises Brent Forecast to $80 as Strait of Hormuz Closure drags on\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Citi lifted its third-quarter Brent projection from $75 to $80 per barrel. The bank, however, retained its fourth-quarter forecast of $70 and continues to expect Brent to average $65 per barrel in 2027. Goldman Sachs has taken a more cautious view than Citi.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/citi-raises-brent-forecast-to-80-as-strait-of-hormuz-closure-drags-on\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Prices Weekly Review: 3rd–7th August 2026\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s downstream petroleum market recorded a broad-based decline in depot prices during the first trading week of August. The downward movement became more pronounced after Dangote Petroleum Refinery reduced its ex-depot prices. The adjustments reflected stronger competition among depot operators, changing replacement-cost expectations and increased pressure to move existing inventories.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-prices-weekly-review-3rd7th-august-2026\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
